00:10:47.153 --> 00:10:50.673
Look, I think the biggest
thing that I tell everybody

00:10:50.673 --> 00:10:52.715
is number one, practicality.

00:10:52.715 --> 00:10:55.583
How much money do you have
to stay alive for how long?

00:10:55.583 --> 00:10:56.654
That is always my biggest fear.

00:10:56.654 --> 00:10:58.164
First-time entrepreneurs
make this mistake.

00:10:58.164 --> 00:11:01.344
Do you have one year's
worth of rent and overhead,

00:11:01.344 --> 00:11:04.236
and then, you have to
make your actions respond

00:11:04.236 --> 00:11:07.663
to your bleeding of cash
before you turn a profit.

00:11:07.663 --> 00:11:08.339
When you start a new business,

00:11:08.339 --> 00:11:10.570
especially an ice cream parlor,

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:13.150
a restaurant, kind of what you're doing,

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.058
you've got to make sure

00:11:14.058 --> 00:11:16.660
that you're putting up upfront investment,

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:17.764
financially, not just time.

00:11:17.764 --> 00:11:19.823
It's not like you're
building something with code,

00:11:19.823 --> 00:11:23.551
you're literally paying rent
and buying supplies, and so,

00:11:23.551 --> 00:11:25.946
you need to have a high
level of practicality.

00:11:25.946 --> 00:11:27.656
The other thing that I tell entrepreneurs

00:11:27.656 --> 00:11:31.233
that are more practical,
